//? Title: Huffman coding: exact merges, checked decoding and logical payload cost
//? Subtitle: Actual heap removals, the original text and the singleton exception
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Build a binary prefix code by repeatedly merging the two least-weight items.
This report follows actual minimum removals and parent insertions, proves the
greedy contraction rule, and retains the original two-sentence text. Exact
integer weights prevent frequency overflow, including when the sum exceeds
uint64. Fully validated byte models reject malformed trees, nonbinary digits and
unfinished codewords. We separate logical payload bits from the ASCII digit
string returned by the API and from codebook/framing costs. Empty and forced
one-bit singleton conventions make the entropy bound's conditions explicit.
)

\toc

> Three symbols, two actual merges

Use counts 5,2,1 for integer symbols 0,1,2. The first minimum pair is 1 and 2,
merged into weight 3. Then 3 and 5 merge into 8. The resulting lengths are
1,2,2, and weighted path cost is5*1+2*2+1*2=11 bits for eight source symbols.
The actual parent weights 3+8 give the same 11. Reading the tree's0/1 branches
yields each prefix word; the root-to-leaf depths explain the lengths.

The native diagram below uses the topology and decimal weights from the
producing execution, not a reconstructed heap history. Leaves are displayed in
actual left-to-right tree order, which differs from input symbol order.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/huffman_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/huffman_analysis.hpp>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <filesystem>
#include <format>
#include <limits>
#include <print>
#include <stdexcept>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    const auto t = dm::algorithms::huffman_counts_trace({5, 2, 1});
    const auto s = dm::algorithms::huffman_summary(t.counts, t.run.lengths);
    std::print("| actual first child | weight | actual second child | weight | new parent | weight |\n| " "---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (const auto &m : t.merges)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", m.left, m.left_weight,
                   m.right, m.right_weight, m.parent, m.parent_weight);
    std::print("\nOriginal-index lengths {}; exact total {}; weighted bits {}; merge cost {}; mean {:.9f}; " "entropy {:.9f}; computed Kraft sum {:.9f}.\n",
               t.run.lengths, t.run.total_weight, t.run.weighted_bits,
               t.run.merge_cost, s.mean_bits, s.entropy_bits, s.kraft_sum);
    dm::algorithms::huffman_tree_diagram(t).save_svg("build/huffman_tiny.svg");
    if (t.run.lengths != std::vector<int>{1, 2, 2} ||
        t.run.weighted_bits != "11" || t.run.merge_cost != "11")
        throw std::runtime_error("tiny construction");
}
