> Derive the greedy rule and its cost identity

For positive weights w_s, a binary prefix tree has cost C=sum_s w_s*l_s. With at
least two symbols an optimal tree can be full: a unary internal node can be
removed to shorten its descendants. A deepest leaf then has a leaf sibling,
since an internal sibling would have an even deeper descendant.

Assign the two smallest weights to such deepest sibling positions. Exchanging a
smaller weight a at depth d_a with a larger weight b at depth d_b>=d_a changes
cost by (a-b)(d_b-d_a)<=0. Thus an optimum exists in which the two smallest
weights are deepest siblings. Contract them into one leaf of weight a+b:

$$C(T)=C(T_{contracted})+a+b.$$
\alttext(Expanding a contracted parent adds one extra bit to each child's weight, increasing cost by their sum.)

An optimal contracted tree must be used, otherwise replacing it would improve
the original tree. Induction therefore justifies the repeated two-minimum merge.
Each leaf weight contributes once for every ancestor, so

$$\sum_s w_s l_s=\sum_{internal\ nodes\ v}w(v).$$
\alttext(Weighted leaf depth equals the sum of all internal parent weights for a tree with at least two leaves.)

The implementation maintains exact nonnegative weights and costs. Its fixed-limb
accumulator covers every representable uint64 count vector on the supported
integer platforms: the total is below 2^128 and even the sum of all possible
parent weights is below 2^192. It does not reject valid counts merely because
their sum exceeds uint64. Leaves are positive symbols in ascending
original-index order; ties break by node creation ID. Byte construction uses
unsigned byte values 0..255, making its choices independent of unordered-map
iteration. This is a deterministic tree rule, not a claimed canonical wire
format.

> Entropy bounds need a singleton convention

Let p_s=w_s/sum w and H=-sum p_s log2(p_s). For prefix lengths, Kraft's sum
K=sum2^(-l_s) is at most 1. Normalize q_s=2^(-l_s)/K. Then

$$\bar l-H=D_2(p\Vert q)-\log_2 K\ge0.$$
\alttext(The weighted mean length exceeds entropy by a nonnegative divergence plus the nonnegative penalty from Kraft sum below one.)

For at least two positive symbols, Shannon lengths ceil(-log2 p_s) are positive
and have mean strictly below H+1. Huffman's optimum cannot cost more, so
H<=mean<H+1. The library deliberately assigns a lone positive symbol the
nonempty word0: H=0 but mean=1=H+1. An empty alphabet has mean/entropy 0 by
reporting convention. Neither exceptional case supports the old unconditional
strict upper-bound claim. Numerical summary fields are rounded diagnostics; the
tree validator and exact integer merge costs supply separate
structural/arithmetic checks.

> Preserve the original text, while distinguishing three storage quantities

The source is the original repeated pangram, including its joining space: 89
ASCII bytes containing 28 distinct byte values. The code counts bytes, not
Unicode characters. The selected original letters and period remain in the
table. All codes and the exact roundtrip come from the same built model.

The encoder returns an ASCII string containing one character per logical0/1
digit. Its character count is the logical payload bit count, but its actual
character storage is not bit-packed. Ceiling(payload_bits/8) is a payload-only
packing estimate, not an archive produced by this API. A decodable file also
needs its codebook and framing, such as a valid-bit count or an agreed
termination rule. Those costs are not included here.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/huffman_original.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/huffman_analysis.hpp>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <filesystem>
#include <format>
#include <limits>
#include <print>
#include <stdexcept>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    const auto text = dm::algorithms::huffman_example_text();
    const auto t = dm::algorithms::huffman_build_trace(text);
    const auto encoded = dm::algorithms::huffman_encode(t.run.code, text);
    const auto decoded = dm::algorithms::huffman_decode(t.run.code, encoded);
    const auto s =
        dm::algorithms::huffman_summary(t.frequencies,
                                        t.run.construction.lengths);
    std::print("| selected byte | frequency | actual codeword | length |\n| --- | ---: | --- | ---: |\n");
    for (char c : {'e', 't', 'o', 'x', 'z', '.'})
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", c,
                   t.frequencies[static_cast<unsigned char>(c)],
                   t.run.code.codes.at(c), t.run.code.codes.at(c).size());
    std::print("\nSource bytes {}; active bytes {}; logical payload bits {}; ASCII digit characters {}; " "payload-only packed-byte estimate {}; original8-bit baseline {}; exact roundtrip " "{}.\n\nEntropy {:.9f}; mean logical bits/byte {:.9f}; computed Kraft sum {:.9f}.\n",
               text.size(), s.active_symbols, encoded.size(), encoded.size(),
               (encoded.size() + 7) / 8, text.size() * 8, decoded == text,
               s.entropy_bits, s.mean_bits, s.kraft_sum);
    std::vector<double> frequency, length;
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < 256; ++i)
        if (t.frequencies[i]) {
            frequency.push_back(t.frequencies[i]);
    length.push_back(t.run.construction.lengths[i]);
        }
        auto left = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
        left.points(frequency, length, "actual byte codes", {37, 99, 235}, 5.).title("Actual lengths versus observed byte frequency").x_label("source frequency").y_label("logical code length").y_limits(0, 9);
        auto right =
            dm::graphics::RPlot::barplot({double(text.size()),
                                          double(encoded.size()),
                                          double((encoded.size() + 7) / 8)},
                                         {"raw source", "ASCII digits",
                                          "packed estimate"}, "payload storage",
                                         {37, 99, 235});
        right.title("Bytes: codebook and framing excluded").y_label(
            "bytes or estimated payload bytes").y_limits(0, 500);
        auto layout = dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2);
        layout.add(left).add(right).size(1250, 620).title(
            "Original pangram: coding cost is not an archive size").fit_panels().save_svg("build/huffman_original.svg");
        if (decoded != text ||
            t.run.construction.weighted_bits != std::to_string(encoded.size()))
            throw std::runtime_error("original roundtrip");
}
