> Six classical weights and a merge-cost proof you can inspect

For weights 45,13,12,16,9,5, the successive parent weights are 14,25,30,55,100.
Their sum 224 equals the exact weighted path cost, so the mean is2.24 bits per
symbol over 100 occurrences. Heap operations below are actual
removals/insertions; no heap contents are regenerated for presentation. The
diagram uses that same producing topology.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/huffman_classic.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/huffman_analysis.hpp>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <filesystem>
#include <format>
#include <limits>
#include <print>
#include <stdexcept>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    const auto t = dm::algorithms::huffman_counts_trace({45, 13, 12, 16, 9, 5});
    const auto s = dm::algorithms::huffman_summary(t.counts, t.run.lengths);
    std::print("| merge | first weight | second weight | parent weight | parent ID |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: " "| ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < t.merges.size(); ++i) {
        const auto &m = t.merges[i];
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", i + 1, m.left_weight,
                   m.right_weight, m.parent_weight, m.parent);
    }
    std::print("\nLengths {}; weighted bits {}; merge cost {}; entropy {:.9f}; mean {:.9f}; actual heap " "pushes {}; pops {}; integer-length tree visits {}.\n",
               t.run.lengths, t.run.weighted_bits, t.run.merge_cost,
               s.entropy_bits, s.mean_bits, t.run.work.heap_pushes,
               t.run.work.heap_pops, t.run.work.tree_visits);
    dm::algorithms::huffman_tree_diagram(t).save_svg("build/huffman_classic.svg");
    if (t.run.weighted_bits != "224" || t.run.merge_cost != "224" ||
        t.merges.size() != 5)
        throw std::runtime_error("classic cost identity");
}
