// result_end
\caption(Huge totals and costs remain exact decimal integers. A logical merge-record policy has different units from a byte/input or output-string limit.)
\alttext(Four bars show equal length2 codewords for four equal maximum uint64 frequencies; table entries separately show empty and forced singleton conventions.)

New run/trace policies default to one million complete borrowed input entries
and one million merge records, each with zero disabling its cap. Count input
entries include zero positions; byte input entries mean source bytes rather than
the fixed 256 histogram slots. The complete known m-1 merge count is admitted
before heap work. Captured input copies, ordinary output topology/lengths,
scalar/decimal metadata and capacity are separate from that record count; it is
not a byte or peak-memory quota. Legacy interfaces have no optional policy caps.
Failure returns no truncated or replayed history. Native tree views apply an
independent complete leaf-display cap and abbreviate only long on-figure weight
labels; exact values remain in the trace.

> Producing work, not a synthetic timing curve

For m positive symbols there are m initial leaf insertions, m-1 parent
insertions, 2(m-1) minimum removals and 2m-1 integer-length node visits. These
are selected producing counts. They exclude heap comparison internals,
exact-integer limb operations, copies, allocation, decimal formatting and
byte-codeword projection. Heap operation counts grow linearly, while
priority-queue comparisons have the familiar O(m log(m+1)) bound. Neither the
plot nor these counters are elapsed-time measurements.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/huffman_work.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/huffman_analysis.hpp>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <filesystem>
#include <format>
#include <limits>
#include <print>
#include <stdexcept>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    std::vector<double> x, heap, visits, records;
    std::print("| positive symbols | actual pushes | actual pops | integer-length visits | actual merge " "records | exact weighted bits |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t m : {2, 4, 8, 16, 32, 64, 128, 256}) {
        const auto t =
            dm::algorithms::huffman_counts_trace(std::vector<std::uint64_t>(
                                                 m, 1));
        const auto &w = t.run.work;
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", m, w.heap_pushes,
                   w.heap_pops, w.tree_visits, t.merges.size(),
                   t.run.weighted_bits);
        x.push_back(m);
        heap.push_back(w.heap_pushes + w.heap_pops);
        visits.push_back(w.tree_visits);
        records.push_back(t.merges.size());
        if (w.heap_pushes != 2 * m - 1 || w.heap_pops != 2 * (m - 1) ||
            w.tree_visits != 2 * m - 1)
            throw std::runtime_error("actual work counts");
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.line(x, heap, "heap operations", {37, 99, 235}, 2.).line(x, visits,
                                                               "node visits",
                                                               {220, 38, 38}, 2.).line(x, records, "merge records", {22, 163, 74}, 2.).title("Equal-weight alphabets: selected producing counts").x_label("positive symbols").y_label("operations, visits or records").y_limits(0, 1250).save_svg("build/huffman_work.svg");
}
